host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan standby -- the ring rebuilt around its loss, and the one repair a ring accepts
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, condense REMEMBER, send the finished increment.
think Standfast first. Read crux/REDS.md whole. Living rows 80, 83, 84, 85 all carry closure notes -- 84 closed 20260819.145920, 85 reopened and closed 20260819.134229 with a real loom standing behind it, 86 and 87 closed as prose notes. Verified the 84 fix on disk rather than trusting the note: .gitignore line 70 does allowlist /crux/. No open agent-closable red, so the constructive queue is clear and this lap opens new work rather than booking a correction.
think Council rota by lap index -- 462 .kyri logs on disk, 462 mod 27 = 3, so the deep-read was foundations/20260811-211431_the-lindy-effect-and-the-long-return.md. Its long-return test shaped what this rung spends its prose on: the README section and the module head are written to still read true after the code moves, and the finding is stated as a sentence a reader can carry rather than as a note about this run.
think The running thread came from the newest log's recommend line: the ring rebuilt around its loss -- whether a declaration may name a standby that legitimately holds the lost domain's regions, and what a grant written for an absent domain costs the ring while it is present. decline.rye had proved no neighbor may reach around a hole; the open question was whether the document itself may draw the detour.
think Read the shape the answer would have to respect before writing any of it. relay.flows_of refuses any region that does not carry exactly one writer and one reader; cycle.ring_order refuses any grant set that does not close on exactly one lap; exercise.store_path addresses a region's backing store by the region's own name; roundtrip.directed_bell_path addresses a bell by the names of both its ends. Those four facts, already proven in earlier rungs, turned out to contain the whole answer -- so this module derives rather than legislates.
think Wrote the two tempting repairs as real declarations and let each refuse itself. serial_cycle_shadow.bron names beech beside birch holding birch's exact grants, so ask_ab has two readers and ask_bc has two writers and the flow derivation returns null -- a refusal a whole layer earlier than any capability check. serial_cycle_bypass.bron answers that honestly by giving dogwood its own arcs, keeping every flow directed, and loses the ring instead: alder spans three peers and no single walk visits all four domains once and comes home.
think That left the repair. serial_cycle_succession.bron names beech where birch stood and moves nothing else -- the same four regions, name for name and byte for byte. Since every attempt in this arc already reloads its document from disk and derives the child's line from that read, handing a later step a later document is the ordinary act the ring has been performing all along. So Assignment gained one field, decl, and nothing else had to change.
think The seam cost was the honest surprise, and it is where the finding earns its second half. A region is addressed by its own name, so a succession inherits every byte standing in one. A bell is addressed by the names of both its ends, so alder->birch and birch->cedar simply cease to exist and alder->beech and beech->cedar stand new at zero. A standby inherits regions and never inherits a bell.
obs Reuse over restatement throughout -- flows_of and peer_span from relay, ring_order and read_plan and the verbs from cycle, the fall and wake wire and the whole child attempt from gap, max_attempts from decline. What standby adds is shape_of (a name for each way a document can fail to be a ring), same_regions (why a succession costs the asks nothing), and the per-step declaration. Nothing already proven was copied.
obs The first metal run failed on an assert rather than on a claim, and the assert was right. I had written succeeded == 4 while the plan carries five carrying steps, because alder places twice under the succession -- once to seat the asks and once to wake its new successor by name. Corrected to 5. A count written from the shape of the idea rather than read off the plan is exactly the memory-over-measurement red the ledger keeps teaching.
obs The bells claim was corrected before it shipped for being true and misleading. The first print read "the succession brings 12 directed bells of its own," which is the total across both documents rather than the succession's own six. Split the report into bells and new_bells so the load-bearing number stands alone, and the line now reads 6 of its own beside the ring's 6.
obs The second RED probe is the one that made the seam cost a fact. Removing alder's wake step and running beech with every one of birch's grants intact produced Unheard and OutcomeMismatch at exit 1 -- so the claim that a standby never inherits a bell is proven on metal rather than asserted from how the path is built. The first probe, a succession renaming ask_ab, was refused for moving a region out from under the asks standing in it, also at exit 1; it fired at the same_regions guard in the check rather than at provision_all's RegionsMoved, which are the same claim held at two depths.
obs Every claim in the new witness reads the selftest output natively with assert out contains, never a shell grep over interpolated output -- REDS #76 and #85, the apostrophe loom, honored by construction in a new witness rather than retrofitted later. The decline and gap witnesses were re-run GREEN afterward, so the two rungs this module imports from are proven unmoved rather than assumed so.
obs REMEMBER stayed single-stranded. The decline edge folded into the prior-edges pointer with its finding kept in two sentences, that pointer itself was condensed from a per-rung wall to one paragraph, and the standby edge seated as the live work-front with its next crux named.
loom witness=caravan_standby_witness result=GREEN declarations=4 refused_shapes=2 attempts_spent=2 declines=1 asks_home=4 asks_home_before_loss=2 bells_standing=6 bells_fresh=6 red_probes=2
file caravan/standby.rye the ring rebuilt around its loss -- two documents refused, one carried home
file caravan/systems/serial_cycle_shadow.bron a standby beside the domain it replaces, refused for two writers on one region
file caravan/systems/serial_cycle_bypass.bron a detour drawn in advance, directed throughout and no longer a ring
file caravan/systems/serial_cycle_succession.bron the same ring declared again, with beech where birch stood
file tools/caravan_standby_witness.rish the witness on metal, both RED paths proven before the green
file caravan/README.md the ladder row and the durable section carrying the finding
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge reseated, the prior edges condensed, the git nib moved
recommend keep-going -- next the two documents standing at once: whether a ring may be re-declared while a lap is in flight rather than only between laps, and what a domain still running under the elder document owes a successor already running under the newer one. standby.rye swaps documents between steps, which is the easy half; the open crux is what happens when the swap lands mid-pass, and whether a supervisor owes every domain a quiescent point before it may hand the ring a new shape. No key, no funds, no provisioning -- agent-doable.
